"This copse, full of strong saplings, each about chest height, continues south and west, where the trees become taller and more densely populated forming a forest of sorts. Northwestward lies a hill which rises up out of the scrub area to the north and northeast, and eastward is a field of golden wheat",
"In this part of the wood, sunlight glints through the leaves high above in the strong, healthy trees. To the north is a hill, with scrub to the northeast and the wood continuing southward and eastward. Westward, however, is a river bank with a considerable drop to the river below",
"The river flows straight across the southern edge of this part of the wood, babbling and burbling its way down to the sea. To the east lies a golden wheatfield with more of the wood northward and westward",
